/// Chapter 8 of the guide, written from md-docs/08-components.md by
/// scripts/site-from-guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page ComponentsChapter(path: "/docs/guide/components", title: "Components", description: "Declaring components: props, enum props, events, slots and scoped slots, parts, local state and stores.", layout: DocsShell("Components", chapter: "Chapter 8", blurb: "A component is a reusable element you declare: typed props, events, slots, parts and a body, checked like a built-in.", sections: [Anchor(id: "declaring-and-calling", label: "Declaring and calling"), Anchor(id: "enum-props", label: "Enum props"), Anchor(id: "events", label: "Events"), Anchor(id: "slots", label: "Slots"), Anchor(id: "parts", label: "Parts"), Anchor(id: "local-state-and-actions", label: "Local state and actions"), Anchor(id: "using-stores-inside-a-component", label: "Using stores inside a component"), Anchor(id: "components-in-the-static-paint", label: "Components in the static paint")], prevTo: "/docs/guide/control-flow", prevLabel: "7. Control flow", nextTo: "/docs/guide/stores", nextLabel: "9. Stores")) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("A component is a reusable element you declare: typed props, the events it fires, the slots its caller fills, the parts it offers, and a body. A call to it is checked like a call to a built-in.")

        Heading("Declaring and calling", id: "declaring-and-calling").h2

        CodeBlock("/// A person, at a glance.\ncomponent UserCard(_ name: String, role: String, active: Bool = true, avatar: String? = null) \{\n    Card.elevated \{\n        Row(align: .center, gap: .md) \{\n            if let src = avatar \{ Avatar(src: src, alt: name) \} else \{ Avatar(initials: name.slice(0, 2)).primary \}\n            Stack \{\n                Text(name).bold\n                Text(role).muted\n            \}\n            if active \{ Badge(\"Active\").success \}\n        \}\n    \}\n\}\n\npage Team(path: \"/\") \{\n    UserCard(\"Monzer\", role: \"Developer\")\n    UserCard(\"Sam\", role: \"Designer\", active: false, avatar: \"/sam.png\")\n    UserCard(\"Ann\", role: \"PM\").active\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("- `_ name: Type` marks the one prop a call may pass positionally; it must be first. Every other prop is passed by name.\n- Prop types: `String`, `Number`, `Bool`, `Map`, `Any`, `[T]`, `T?`, or a declared `type` or `enum`. They must be written; `= expr` gives a default, and a `T?` defaults to `null`.\n- A `Bool` prop is set with a flag: `.active`. An enum prop with a flag or by name: `.loud` or `tone: .loud`.\n- A `///` comment above the component or a prop is its documentation.\n\nA prop that reads the caller's state stays live inside the component: a `Chip(pressed: isOn)` repaints when `isOn` changes.")

        Heading("Enum props", id: "enum-props").h2

        CodeBlock("enum Tone \{ calm, loud \}\n\ncomponent Note(_ text: String, tone: Tone = .calm) \{\n    Text(text) \{\n        style \{ padding: $sm; border-radius: $radius-sm \}\n    \}\n\}\n\npage Notes(path: \"/\") \{\n    Note(\"Quiet\")\n    Note(\"Loud!\", tone: .loud)\n    Note(\"Loud too\").loud\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("A component's enum props are written to its root element as `data-<prop>=\"<case>\"` — `data-tone=\"loud\"` — so a stylesheet can select on them: `.note[data-tone=\"loud\"] \{ font-weight: 700 \}`.")

        Heading("Events", id: "events").h2

        Markdown("A component declares the events it fires with `event name(param: Type)`, fires them with `emit name(value)`, and the caller handles them with `on name(value) \{ \}`:")

        CodeBlock("type Todo \{ id: String, title: String, done: Bool = false \}\n\ncomponent TodoRow(_ todo: Todo) \{\n    event toggle(id: String)\n    event remove(id: String)\n    Row(align: .center, gap: .sm) \{\n        Checkbox(checked: todo.done, label: todo.title) \{ on change \{ emit toggle(todo.id) \} \}\n        IconButton(icon: \"trash\", label: \"Remove \{todo.title\}\").sm \{ on click \{ emit remove(todo.id) \} \}\n    \}\n\}\n\npage Todos(path: \"/\") \{\n    state todos: [Todo] = [Todo(id: \"1\", title: \"Milk\"), Todo(id: \"2\", title: \"Eggs\")]\n    action toggle(id: String) \{\n        todos = todos.map(t => if t.id == id \{ Todo(id: t.id, title: t.title, done: !t.done) \} else \{ t \})\n    \}\n    for t in todos by t.id \{\n        TodoRow(t) \{\n            on toggle(id) \{ toggle(id) \}\n            on remove(id) \{ todos = todos.filter(t => t.id != id) \}\n        \}\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("The checker holds `emit` to the declared parameters (`T09`) and a handler on a call to a declared event or a DOM event; a DOM event on a component call attaches to its root element.")

        Heading("Slots", id: "slots").h2

        Markdown("A component places its caller's block with `children`, and may declare named slots the caller fills with `name \{ … \}`:")

        CodeBlock("component Panel(_ title: String) \{\n    slot\n    slot trailing\n    Card \{\n        Row(justify: .between, align: .center) \{\n            Heading(title).h3\n            trailing\n        \}\n        children\n    \}\n\}\n\npage Keys(path: \"/\") \{\n    Panel(\"API keys\") \{\n        trailing \{ Badge(\"Beta\").info \}\n        Text(\"Rotate every 90 days.\")\n        Button(\"Generate\").primary\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("`slot` declares the default slot (`children`); `slot trailing` a named one. A fill is compiled in the caller's scope — it reads the caller's state and loop variables — and the component only decides where it lands. A page's `layout:` is a component with a default slot, called with the page as its block.")

        Heading("Scoped slots", id: "scoped-slots").h3

        Markdown("A slot may hand values to its fill. The component declares what it hands, uses the slot with those values by name, and the caller's fill names them in order:")

        CodeBlock("type Todo \{ id: String, title: String, done: Bool = false \}\n\ncomponent TodoList(items: [Todo]) \{\n    slot row(item: Todo, index: Number)\n    slot empty\n    if items.length == 0 \{\n        empty\n    \} else \{\n        for it, i in items by it.id \{ row(item: it, index: i) \}\n    \}\n\}\n\npage Use(path: \"/\") \{\n    state todos: [Todo] = [Todo(id: \"1\", title: \"Milk\")]\n    TodoList(items: todos) \{\n        row(t, i) \{ Text(\"\{i + 1\}. \{t.title\}\") \}\n        empty \{ Text(\"Nothing to do.\").muted \}\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("The fill's names are typed by the declaration (`t` is a `Todo`), and the fill is drawn again when a value it is handed changes.")

        Heading("Parts", id: "parts").h2

        Markdown("A component may declare parts — components of its own, called under its name, the way `Card.Header` is a part of `Card`:")

        CodeBlock("component Panel(_ title: String) \{\n    part Header(_ text: String) \{ Heading(text).h3 \}\n    part Footer \{ Divider  Text(\"End\").muted.sm \}\n    Card \{ Text(title)  children \}\n    slot\n\}\n\npage Parts(path: \"/\") \{\n    Panel(\"Keys\") \{\n        Panel.Header(\"Rotate\")\n        Text(\"Body\")\n        Panel.Footer\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Markdown("A part is declared inside the component and has props, events and slots of its own; a part declares no parts.")

        Heading("Local state and actions", id: "local-state-and-actions").h2

        Markdown("A component has its own `state`, `derived`, `effect`, actions, timers and handles; each instance gets its own:")

        CodeBlock("component Stepper(_ start: Number, step: Number = 1) \{\n    event change(value: Number)\n    state n = start\n    derived even = n % 2 == 0\n    action move(by: Number) \{ n = n + by  emit change(n) \}\n    Row(gap: .sm, align: .center) \{\n        Button(\"−\").sm \{ on click \{ move(-step) \} \}\n        Text(\"\{n\}\").bold\n        Button(\"+\").sm \{ on click \{ move(step) \} \}\n        if even \{ Badge(\"even\").info \}\n    \}\n\}", title: "wf")

        Heading("Using stores inside a component", id: "using-stores-inside-a-component").h2

        Markdown("`use StoreName` brings a store into a component as it does a page:")

        CodeBlock("store Cart \{\n    state items: [String] = []\n    action add(name: String) \{ items.push(name) \}\n\}\n\ncomponent AddToCart(_ name: String) \{\n    use Cart\n    Button(\"Add \{name\}\").primary \{ on click \{ Cart.add(name) \} \}\n\}\n\npage Shop(path: \"/\") \{\n    use Cart\n    AddToCart(\"Pen\")\n    Text(\"\{Cart.items.length\} in cart\")\n\}", title: "wf")

        Heading("Components in the static paint", id: "components-in-the-static-paint").h2

        Markdown("A static build expands every component call into HTML at build time — its props substituted, its slots filled, its loops and branches over seeded state painted — so a page built from components is a real page before any script runs.")
    }
}
